{
"cells": [
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"# Human Activity Recognition (HAR) - Model Training\n",
"This notebook trains a lightweight neural network for classifying human activities (e.g., stationary vs. walking) using accelerometer data, designed for deployment on an ESP32 microcontroller."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"import tensorflow as tf\n",
"import numpy as np\n",
"import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
"\n",
"print("TensorFlow Version:", tf.version)"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"## 1. Generate Synthetic HAR Dataset\n",
"For demonstration purposes, we simulate windowed accelerometer readings (50 samples per window, 3 axes: X, Y, Z)."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"np.random.seed(42)\n",
"num_samples = 1000\n",
"window_size = 50\n",
"num_channels = 3\n",
"\n",
"# Class 0: Stationary (low variance), Class 1: Walking (high variance/periodic)\n",
"X_class_0 = np.random.normal(0, 0.5, (num_samples // 2, window_size, num_channels))\n",
"X_class_1 = np.random.normal(0, 2.5, (num_samples // 2, window_size, num_channels))\n",
"\n",
"X = np.vstack((X_class_0, X_class_1))\n",
"y = np.array([0] * (num_samples // 2) + [1] * (num_samples // 2))\n",
"\n",
"# Shuffle dataset\n",
"indices = np.arange(num_samples)\n",
"np.random.shuffle(indices)\n",
"X = X[indices]\n",
"y = y[indices]\n",
"\n",
"# Train/Test Split\n",
"split = int(0.8 * num_samples)\n",
"X_train, X_test = X[:split], X[split:]\n",
"y_train, y_test = y[:split], y[split:]\n",
"\n",
"print("Training data shape:", X_train.shape)\n",
"print("Testing data shape:", X_test.shape)"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"## 2. Build Lightweight Neural Network Architecture\n",
"We use a compact Flatten + Dense architecture or 1D Conv suitable for low-memory microcontrollers."
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"model = tf.keras.Sequential([\n",
"    tf.keras.layers.Input(shape=(window_size, num_channels)),\n",
"    tf.keras.layers.Flatten(),\n",
"    tf.keras.layers.Dense(16, activation='relu'),\n",
"    tf.keras.layers.Dense(1, activation='sigmoid')\n",
"])\n",
"\n",
"model.compile(optimizer='adam',\n",
"              loss='binary_crossentropy',\n",
"              metrics=['accuracy'])\n",
"\n",
"model.summary()"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"## 3. Train the Model"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"metadata": {},
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"history = model.fit(X_train, y_train,\n",
"                    epochs=15,\n",
"                    batch_size=32,\n",
"                    validation_data=(X_test, y_test))"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "markdown",
"metadata": {},
"source": [
"## 4. Save Keras Model"
]
},
{
"cell_type": "code",
"execution_count": null,
"outputs": [],
"source": [
"model.save('har_model.h5')\n",
"print("Model saved successfully as har_model.h5")"
]
}
],
